      "writtenOn": "2022-12-09T06:37:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Wait I am confused. You require all methods to be called on one thread but you also require a looper to be passed ?\n\nIt seems you only read the mLooper variable in ensureCurrentThread. So instead of a looper, I suggest you have something like :\n\n    private final Thread mMyThread;\n    ...\n    public SyncStateMachine(final String name, final boolean dbg) {\n      ...\n      mMyThread \u003d Thread.currentThread()\n    }\n    ...\n    public void ensureCorrectThread() {\n      if (!mMyThread.equals(Thread.currentThread()) throw ISE()\n    }\n\nThis means you *must* create the object on the same thread where it\u0027s used. If that\u0027s inconvenient, you might say that the caller must declare its intention of running this on the given thread by passing an instance of Thread instead of an instance of Looper, but then you need to be very very careful about the threading visibility of any non-final member – e.g. mInitialState (there is not enough context in this patch to know if it will be fine). Hint : this is not actually feasible without locking (if your final implementation must either have locks or require the constructor is called on the same thread, or it\u0027s necessarily incorrect).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 87,
        "startChar": 47,
        "endLine": 87,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "b37e00b19eba194a98a44c49cb7aa2b5f8421728",
